# Pirate Shores Security Lab

A Flask web app I’m building to better understand how web apps work while learning cybersecurity.

## Overview
This project is me learning by building. I’m starting simple, then I’ll be breaking it (SQL injection, brute force, etc) and fixing it so I actually understand how these attacks work while learning Python, Flask and HTML.

## Current Features
- Login page with Flask  
- SQLite database to store user credentials  
- Uses POST requests  
- App checks if credentials match  
- Password hashing  
- User-specific homepage
- Login.log form that stoes login attempts 
- brute force dectector
- roles, can only access some pages depending on your role

## Why I’m doing this
- To actually understand how login systems work  
- To learn cybersecurity by testing things myself  
- To get comfortable with backend logic and how data flows  

## Tech
- Python
- Flask
- HTML
- SQLite
- Hashlib
- Sessions

